Operator 2026-06-13: fold in detection/verification use; assess whether the
weights can save us from brute-force training or be introspected for drastic
improvement.

UC2 (detection): diffusion gives a variational likelihood BOUND (not exact AR
logprob) BUT a BIDIRECTIONAL per-token surprisal p(x_i|x_\i) -- a native
error-localization signal stronger than left-only AR perplexity, valuable in the
NON-executable regime where execution verifiers can't reach. Gate: per-position-
logits precondition + cheap AUROC-vs-AR-perplexity probe. Promising-with-precedent,
not proven; learned-tier, not a moat improvement.

UC3 (weights): honest separation -
  REAL: the pretrained diffusion score = -grad E is a free gradient-accessible
  energy-PRIOR -> composing it with the verifier energy at inference could SHORTCUT
  Phase-3's 'train our own deep EBM' (frozen-score composition, not weight
  extraction; discrete-gradient relaxations have Q11/STE sharp edges).
  PLAUSIBLE: activation probing/steering (modest, needs a fitted probe) + entropy-
  targeted verification efficiency.
  SPECULATIVE (do NOT bet): closed-form weight extraction / drastic improvement by
  pure introspection -- not technically supported; flagged so we don't chase a Beachhead.

Still queued/non-competing; UC1 gated on the TRM graft.

